#{[17592186351408 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186351101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351408 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82286" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351408 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351408 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351408 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2eb579cc-338e-51a2-b3da-e05dcf5ef478" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351408 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|A|=(-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1=-\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|C|=4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2=-8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351409 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351409 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82289" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351409 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351409 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351409 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dec8cece-e79e-5652-812a-3c79c57417e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351409 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is a diagonal matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 3=-24\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82290" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- $A$ has two identical rows\n- $A$ has a zero row" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8066ca0-5e8f-5876-924e-8be55bf1f74e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351410 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor a zero row.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400867 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400867 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140046" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400867 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400867 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400867 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c1bd5a4-43fd-5d63-843c-209b976b49d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400867 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The $A$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|A|=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1\\cdot 4=8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has identical columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(C)=5\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot (-10)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400868 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400868 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400868 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400868 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400868 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400868 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400868 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400868 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186400870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400868 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d252fa00-ae50-5d73-8bce-ecc15224f399" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400869 #edb/ref 1080 "$|B|$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400869 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921864