0350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420350 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420350 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420350 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420350 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ff922856-e3c4-5b40-8d0e-cd85fae942ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420351 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420351 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82285" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420351 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420351 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}6 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420351 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2642af15-1045-5d0f-97c1-3ce034155f08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420351 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn. \n\n- The matrix $A$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420352 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420352 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82192" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420352 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420352 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $7det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -0.5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420352 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "89fae1b5-1405-51b4-b87d-75b6acbbdc2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420352 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(B)=3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1\\cdot 2=-6\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7det(A)-2det(B)=7\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-6)=12.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420353 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420353 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42463" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420353 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420353 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has identical rows\n- $A$ has proportional columns\n- $A$ has a zero row" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420353 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d2486be8-75b8-51f1-882e-08f8a79961f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420353 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
